%% Sequence diagram 3: receiving a purchase order, and the stock-out alert clearing on the next read.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor I as Inventory & Procurement Manager
  participant B as Browser (Vue page)
  participant C as API controller /api/v1
  participant IS as InventoryService
  participant AS as AlertService
  participant RS as RecommendationService
  participant D as MySQL / MariaDB

  I->>B: Receive stock on order PO-n (quantity, expiry)
  B->>C: POST /purchase-orders/{id}/receive + CSRF token
  C->>C: role = inventory?
  C->>IS: receive_purchase_order(outlet, id, lines, user)
  IS->>D: SELECT purchase order FOR UPDATE
  IS->>IS: status receivable? each qty <= outstanding? expiry >= received date?
  alt invalid
    IS-->>C: ValidationError / ConflictError
    C-->>B: 422 / 409, error shown next to the line
  else valid
    loop each received line
      IS->>D: INSERT stock_batches (linked to the order)
      IS->>D: INSERT stock_movements (stock_in, reference = purchase_order)
      IS->>D: UPDATE line qty_received
    end
    IS->>D: UPDATE order status (partially_received / received), audit log, COMMIT
    IS-->>C: updated order
    C-->>B: 200
  end
  I->>B: open Dashboard
  B->>C: GET /alerts?status=open
  C->>AS: list_alerts(outlet, role)
  opt last evaluation older than 60 s (or Run alert check)
  AS->>AS: evaluate(outlet) (idempotent)
  AS->>RS: requirements and reorder suggestions for today
  AS->>IS: usable stock, expiring batches
  AS->>D: close alerts whose condition no longer holds, open new ones
  end
  AS-->>C: open alerts for this role
  C-->>B: 200, the stock-out alert is gone
